 synthesis with explicit helper loss","locator":"04-classical-synthesis.tex:3–111, 1012–1119; thm:classical-synthesis, eq:synthesis-energy","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-synthesis","statement":"For every fixed finite bounded smooth odd seed-only exclusion formula with one unused positive-probability helper type per rank, and every η>0, a finite seeded circuit has insertion v with ‖1_{H^c}(v−v_cl)‖<η and |E(v)−E(m)|≤2η+2√p_H. Here m=Σ_c1_c sin(2θ_c), the ideal classical rotation has its stated spin decomposition, and all circuit angles are independent of D,n,J.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.seeded_synthesis","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation%22%2C%22circuit.seeded_synthesis%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation%22%2C%22circuit.seeded_synthesis%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.seeded_synthesis"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.ordinary_word_positive","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.ordinary_word_positive%22%2C%22circuit.seeded_synthesis%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges/%5B%22circuit.ordinary_word_positive%22%2C%22circuit.seeded_synthesis%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":